40
00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:43.050
Jenna and Angela, you are both incredible multi-hyphenates, so we imagine a lot goes into keeping everything moving.

41
00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:46.730
When you told me they called us multi-hyphenates, you know I had to look it up.

42
00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:46.950
Yeah.

43
00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:56.390
Okay, so according to the Cambridge Dictionary, a multi-hyphenate is someone who does several different jobs, especially in the entertainment industry.

44
00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:59.570
For example, we are actor-writer-podcasters.

45
00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:00.210
Yeah.

46
00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:01.510
I would add producers.

47
00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:02.090
Yeah.

48
00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:03.790
And we run our own business.

49
00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:04.290
Yeah.

50
00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:04.850
What else?

51
00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:06.010
We scrapbook.

52
00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:08.370
Is that in the entertainment industry?

53
00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:09.790
We love a good sale.

54
00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.030
That's probably shopping.

55
00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:12.710
I don't know.

56
00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:15.110
I would count it as part of our multi-hyphenates.

57
00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:20.090
Well, Angela, Buick is bringing everyone a challenge to make the best of their Mondays.

58
00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:25.070
So they want to know, do we have any rituals that kick off our week?

59
00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:30.570
And are you more of a Monday motivation person or a Friday feeling person?

60
00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:33.390
I mean, I'm not really sure what they mean by Monday motivation.

61
00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:36.590
Is that like someone who's like, let's go and tackle the week.

62
00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:40.730
We're going to hit the ground running on Monday because that is definitely not me.

63
00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:41.230
That is not you.

64
00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:42.110
I am not that.

65
00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:43.810
I am more of a Friday feeling person.

66
00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:44.270
Yeah.

67
00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:48.030
Everyone who listens to Office Ladies probably knew that.

68
00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:49.510
Well, I don't know.

69
00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:50.110
Is that shade?

70
00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:51.090
Are you throwing shade at me?

71
00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:52.250
I'm not throwing you shade.

72
00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:53.390
No, not at all.

73
00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:56.410
I'm sure it's no surprise that I'm a Monday motivation person.

74
00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:58.270
This is why we're such a great team.

75
00:02:58.370 --> 00:02:59.170
It really is.

76
00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:01.750
And I definitely have rituals that kick off my week.

77
00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:03.610
We work mostly from home.

78
00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:09.270
And a lot of what I struggle with is ignoring house chores when I'm supposed to be working.

79
00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:10.110
Yeah.

80
00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:10.750
Yeah.

81
00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:16.890
So I actually like to do things on Sunday evening to set myself up for success on Monday.

82
00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:20.090
So my Monday motivation starts on Sunday.

83
00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:21.030
Of course it does.

84
00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:23.230
Your Monday motivation starts on the weekend.

85
00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:24.110
That's so perfect.

86
00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:25.370
Here are some examples.

87
00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:30.210
I always make sure that we've done all the dishes so that I wake up to a clean sink.

88
00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:32.030
I have to wake up to a clean sink.

89
00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:33.330
This makes me very happy.

90
00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:33.810
Okay.

91
00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:36.930
We do all of our grocery shopping and meal planning over the weekend.

92
00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:40.770
And I like to have a clean home office on Monday morning.

93
00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:45.410
Like I'll even write down a list of priorities for my week in a notepad,

94
00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:48.250
and I'll put it on my desk next to my computer on Sunday night.

95
00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:50.930
This is how I set myself up for a great Monday.

96
00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:52.650
I mean, I know this about you.

97
00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:56.430
And I also know if one of those things doesn't happen, things can get walking.

98
00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:57.130
Oh, I lose it.

99
00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.250
I lose it.

100
00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:00.730
Well, I'm definitely more of a Friday feeling person.

101
00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:04.550
And I feel like I need something to work towards, you know,

102
00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:07.590
like that light at the end of the tunnel kind of thing to keep me motivated.

103
00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:11.210
And I have found with myself, if I think about like the big picture,

104
00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:14.470
like everything I have to do that day or everything I have to do that week,

105
00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:15.390
I get overwhelmed.

106
00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:17.790
So I really just have to take it one day at a time.

107
00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:21.970
I set little like daily goals for myself, and then I get a little reward.

108
00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:23.230
Oh, like what?

109
00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:25.070
I mean, it doesn't have to be anything big.

110
00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:27.570
Like I'll work a long day and then say, you know what?

111
00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:31.550
I'm going to go for a nice walk, and I'm going to look at flowers,

112
00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:33.990
and I'm going to just let my mind wander.

113
00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:35.770
I mean, I'm not exercising.

114
00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:36.650
You understand this.

115
00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:37.710
Like this isn't like I'm...

116
00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.990
Nobody thought you were exercising.

117
00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:40.030
Don't worry.

118
00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:41.670
I'm not going to burn any calories.

119
00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:44.170
But that walk is like my mental break.

120
00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.170
I'm kind of the opposite of you, Angela.

121
00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:48.030
I have to take my walk first thing in the morning.

122
00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:51.950
I find that I can quiet my brain if I work my body.

123
00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:55.730
But what I do each morning to set myself up for a great day of work,

124
00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:57.630
it also depends on what kind of work we're doing.

125
00:04:57.910 --> 00:04:59.950
For example, if we're working on our book,

126
00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:03.590
I have this little routine that I call my mental warm-ups.

127
00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:05.770
And I developed this from like...

128
00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:08.850
I mean, listen, lady, I listen to all these podcasts of like

129
00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:13.150
people who have suggestions on how to like organize your life.

130
00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:13.950
You know I love them.

131
00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:14.710
You love that.

132
00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.650
You love like how to be successful five steps.

133
00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:18.290
I do.

134
00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:19.950
For every successful person.

135
00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:20.950
You love all that stuff.

136
00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:21.370
Oh, yeah.

137
00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.890
So here's what I came up with.

138
00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:28.610
I do 15 minutes of reading and then 15 minutes of journaling.

139
00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:29.550
I set a timer.

140
00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:35.470
But during that time, I keep a notepad next to me and I write down anything that jumps in my mind.

141
00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:40.850
Like it might be an idea for writing later, but it might be a chore or an email that I need to

142
00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:41.170
return.

143
00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:46.650
So I jot it down and then I let it kind of flow through me and I keep reading and I keep journaling.

144
00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:50.550
And then when I'm done, I look at my list and I prioritize it.

145
00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:55.170
I say what really needs to be done from this list before I start writing and what can wait.

146
00:05:55.530 --> 00:06:01.670
And somehow getting it down on the paper, it's this way where I've tricked my brain into knowing

147
00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:04.390
that it'll get done, but I can let it go for now.

148
00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:05.950
And it doesn't have to sit in my brain.

149
00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:09.130
It doesn't have to keep reminding me to do it because it's on the paper now.

150
00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:09.770
Right, right.

151
00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:13.950
So that will really set me up for a great day of intense writing.

152
00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:15.030
I like that.

153
00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:19.670
But I think that's just you practicing self-care because I know we've been friends a long time

154
00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:23.370
that sometimes if you get a thought in your head, you've got to do something with it.

155
00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:23.610
Yeah.

156
00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:25.410
You can't just let it spin around up there.

157
00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:26.890
Containment is hard for me.

158
00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.390
Well, I think you're doing a great job.

159
00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:37.610
You know, Jenna, because I've sent you countless photos of me with my coffee mug on my back porch.

160
00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:40.530
I start my day by sitting on my porch.

161
00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:41.730
It's really simple.

162
00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:46.670
I mean, gosh, sometimes I only get to sit for five minutes, maybe 10 minutes, but it

163
00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:48.150
just feeds my soul.

164
00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:50.630
And I don't know if it's like a Southern thing.

165
00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:54.210
Every one of my family at some point in the day sits on their porch.

166
00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:58.630
And my dad used to say, find yourself a thinking spot and take a moment.

167
00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.370
And it just makes me feel good.

168
00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:03.870
So I guess my thinking spot is my back porch.

169
00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:06.910
And I like to just have my cup of tea.

170
00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:11.350
I'm a big tea drinker, you know, and I sort of listen to the birds chatter.

171
00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:17.830
And it's like my moment of calm before kids and school and life and work and all of that

172
00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:19.070
just kicks into high gear.

173
00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:23.890
And I live for those few moments in the morning and on days that I don't get it because, you

174
00:07:23.890 --> 00:07:27.030
know, you don't always get to have that little self-care moment.

175
00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:27.390
Oh, yeah.

176
00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:29.590
I don't quite feel like myself, you know.

177
00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:35.590
So it's a really small act of self-care that took me years to figure out how much it means

178
00:07:35.590 --> 00:07:35.990
to me.

179
00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:40.750
And it's just really a gift that I love to be able to make for myself in the morning.

180
00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:45.030
But guess what day is my favorite day of the week?

181
00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:46.390
Friday feeling.

182
00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:47.110
Friday.

183
00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:50.070
Because I try to give myself a double reset.

184
00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:53.330
So I have my morning porch time, right, with my cup of tea.

185
00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:59.170
And then on Fridays, after I've worked my full day, I love to catch a little bit of the sunset,

186
00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:01.590
sit on the back porch with a glass of wine.

187
00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:03.970
And that I look forward to all week.

188
00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:05.430
That's my Friday feeling moment.

189
00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:10.150
Lady, this is really making me want to be you because that just all sounds lovely.

190
00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:12.910
Well, I was actually thinking, you know what?

191
00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:16.690
While I'm sitting out there having my cup of tea and listening to the birds, maybe if I

192
00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:21.050
took a little notepad with me, I could jot down some of the things I wanted to do that

193
00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:21.310
day.

194
00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.490
And then I would have my list and not forget anything.

195
00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:24.010
Yeah.

196
00:08:24.110 --> 00:08:26.410
Do you see how great this is when you share your rituals?

197
00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:27.030
Yeah.

198
00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:27.930
I like it.

199
00:08:28.370 --> 00:08:30.750
Well, thank you, Buick, for kicking things off.

200
00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:34.510
Later in the episode, we're going to tell you what we think of the Buick and Visions.

201
00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:35.950
Spoiler alert.

202
00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:36.350
Yeah.

203
00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:37.590
We love them.

204
00:08:37.670 --> 00:08:38.330
We love them.

205
00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:39.590
All right.

206
00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:41.330
Should I move on to fast fact number two?

207
00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:41.790
Yeah.

208
00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:47.590
Fast fact number two, we wouldn't be making an Office Ladies podcast if we had not been

209
00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:48.110
on The Office.

210
00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:49.710
Probably not.

211
00:08:49.850 --> 00:08:50.770
We wouldn't know each other.

212
00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:51.950
That is true.

213
00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:53.450
Well, we wouldn't have met.

214
00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:54.830
I didn't even think about that.

215
00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:55.570
That's so sad.

216
00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:56.230
Yeah.

217
00:08:56.230 --> 00:08:58.470
Well, we had a fan question from Michael S.

218
00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:01.610
who asked, when you guys have guests on the

219
00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:04.470
podcast, you always ask them how they got to be on The Office.

220
00:09:04.490 --> 00:09:06.130
But how did you two do it?

221
00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:07.330
Are you kidding me?

222
00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:08.470
Have we not talked about this?

223
00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:14.050
So I went back and we shared a little bit about it in the pilot episode of Office Ladies.

224
00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:14.510
Okay.

225
00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:17.510
But we haven't like talk talked about it.

226
00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:18.850
I feel like there's more to say.

227
00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:19.330
Okay.

228
00:09:19.570 --> 00:09:24.130
So in the pilot, you shared that you had originally auditioned for the role of Pam.

229
00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:24.730
Oh, yeah.

230
00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:27.870
And you didn't get the role, but you did not tell us about auditioning for Angela.

231
00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:29.050
Oh, my gosh.

232
00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:29.930
For Angela Martin?

233
00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:30.970
I'll tell you about it.

234
00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:31.390
Yes.

235
00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:31.670
Okay.

236
00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:33.130
So I auditioned for the role of Pam.

237
00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:34.730
They said I was too feisty.

238
00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:35.610
Bye-bye.

239
00:09:36.770 --> 00:09:38.390
But they said they liked me.

240
00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:39.610
But you know, you hear that.

241
00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:40.270
You hear that.

242
00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:42.690
But you're like, okay, but does that mean I'll ever get called back?

243
00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:44.690
I just, I had to keep on moving.

244
00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:45.110
Yeah.

245
00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:45.870
You kept going.

246
00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:46.410
Kept going.

247
00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:47.110
That's what you do.

248
00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:48.410
You just go to the next audition.

249
00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:48.990
That's right.

250
00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:53.470
You know, they say in Hollywood that the overnight success, you know, you've heard that expression,

251
00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:53.670
right?

252
00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:53.890
Yeah.

253
00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:55.030
Oh, she's an overnight success.

254
00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:58.770
I don't know who came up with that because my overnight success was nine years.

